<title>USA: IBM says Vermont plant may hire 700 temps.</title>
<headline>IBM says Vermont plant may hire 700 temps.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1996-11-08</dateline>
<text>
<p>International Business Machines said its plant in Essex Junction, Vermont, may hire as many as 700 temporary workers next year due to rising worldwide demand for computer chips.</p>
<p>Spokesman Jeff Couture added the latest employee buyout offer has helped the company avoid layoffs at the plant, which it was considering only two months ago.</p>
<p>--U.S. Municipal Desk, 212-859-1650</p>
</text>
